You grade 5 answers to one task about a git repository.
For each criterion listed and each answer, decide pass (true) or fail (false) and give a one-line reason.
Use the ground truth for every number. A criterion that asks for a hedge passes only when the answer hedges.
Reply with ONLY a JSON object: {"A": [{"n": 1, "pass": true, "reason": "..."}], "B": [{"n": 1, "pass": true, "reason": "..."}], "C": [{"n": 1, "pass": true, "reason": "..."}], "D": [{"n": 1, "pass": true, "reason": "..."}], "E": [{"n": 1, "pass": true, "reason": "..."}]}
with one entry per listed criterion, using its number n (1, 2, 3, 4, 5).

TASK PROMPT:
Does anyone show up in this repo's history under more than one name or email? If so, fix it so each person is counted once, then tell me the new top author.

